# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0010033> (generalized peeling skin syndrome)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:263543") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0010033> "Generalized peeling skin syndrome (PSS) is a form of PSS presenting with a generalized distribution. It comprises two sub-types: the non-inflammatory (PSS type A) and the inflammatory (PSS type B) form. PSS type A is characterized by generalized white scaling with superficial peeling of the skin, while PSS type B is characterized by superficial patchy peeling of the entire skin with underlying erythroderma, associated with pruritus, and atopy.")
