AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "Wikipedia:Hyper-IgM_syndrome_type_1") rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0010626> "This variant of the hyper-IgM syndrome is caused by mutation of the CD40LG gene. The genetic locus for this gene is Xq26. This gene codes for the CD40 ligand, which is expressed on T cells. When the CD40 ligand binds CD40 on B cells, then the B cell switches from producing IgM to producing IgA or IgG.")
